{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChFQ8ESNj7cfBz8DUwzAc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed all five review findings, each with a test that failed first. The full `npm test` run passed with exit 0 and no failures, and lint is clean. Everything is committed except `.redeye/notes.md`.\n\n1. **Resume skipped the install command.** I moved the install step into a helper, `installDeps`, in `src/orchestrator.ts`. A resumed ticket now runs it in the recreated worktree before the loop starts, the same as a fresh one. A new test in `review-integration` resumes with an install command set and checks that it ran.\n\n2. **Review-log commits raced with other tickets' commits.** `commitProgress` in `src/progress.ts` now runs commits one at a time, the same way `worktreeQueue` works. The other commit made in the base checkout, `commitTicketFiles`, now goes through it too, so it waits its turn. A new test in `progress` makes 8 commits at once: before the fix they failed on `.git/index.lock`, now all succeed and nothing is left uncommitted.\n\n3. **The review log recorded the config's implement string after a command-line override.** `resolveRoles` now also returns `implementStr`. Without an override it is the config string. With one, it is the command-line provider and its flags written out as a role string (for example `claude -m sonnet`), via a new `renderRoleString`. `index.ts` passes that into the loop. I added a test in `config`, and the existing override test in `integration` now also checks the review log. The \"X overrides implement (…)\" message still shows the config string on purpose.\n\n4. **Resume ignored a recorded failing test gate.** `detectResume` no longer resumes when the last round recorded `testResult: 'fail'`, so the ticket starts fresh. A new test checks that implementation runs again and the branch with failing tests is not merged.\n\n5. **The review role got `--prefer-subagent` on providers that don't support it.** `resolveRoles` now drops it from any role, implement or review, whose provider is not claude. It returns one warning per provider, which `index.ts` prints in place of the old implement-only check, with the same wording. `--max-turns` needed no change: `spawnAgent` already warns and drops it for non-claude providers on every spawn.\n\nThings to know:\n- Findings 1 and 4 are in one commit because they change the same function and share a new test helper. The other findings each have their own commit.\n- Routing ticket-checklist commits through `commitProgress` left an import unused in `orchestrator.ts`, so I removed it to keep lint passing.\n- I added two rules to `AGENTS.md`: base-checkout commits must go through the queue, and a resumed worktree needs the install command. I also extended the existing provider-options rule to say where each option gets dropped.\n- `tsc --noEmit` reports type errors in `test/display.test.ts`. I didn't change that file and didn't touch them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":271,"cache_read_input_tokens":113580,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":271},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa892f86-2174-49d3-8cef-7c815fe9f7e8","uuid":"9f1cb120-1e9f-44fd-b6d4-1ed00da762f0","timestamp":"2026-11-21T03:56:03.502Z","request_id":"req_011ChFQ8EHTFhLyjfiqM6PSN"}
